    ┌─ Thora's story ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │                                                                                                   │
    │  Your parents were plain folk who worked, ate, slept, and did not talk about it. You came in a    │
    │  hard winter, when the river froze to its bed, and you came early and small.                      │
    │                                                                                                   │
    │  A winter wolf came into the yard when you were six, and you faced it with a stick until the      │
    │  grown folk came. The story grew; so did you. You worked, as everyone worked, and nothing of it   │
    │  is worth the telling.                                                                            │
    │                                                                                                   │
    │  Your family died owing, and you worked the debt off a shilling at a time, and learned what       │
    │  every shilling was worth. Fortune never found your door; whatever you have, you got yourself.    │
    │                                                                                                   │
    │  You left, as the young do, because staying was the one thing you could not bear. You came to     │
    │  the Hall by the road everyone comes by.                                                          │
    │                                                                                                   │
